'' A NESTED LIST IN AN INITIALISER FILLS ITS OWN FIELD AND PADS IT -- '( ( 1 ), 3 )' is p = ( 1, 0 ),
'' z = 3, and '{ ( 1 ), ( 2, 3 ) }' element by element. tiko flattened values and fields and paired
'' them by position, silently shifting later values, in shared, static and module-level forms.
'' Expected output is fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/init-nested-align.bas -o tests/codegen/initnestedalign.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/initnestedalign.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 0 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  120056
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 0 2 3 4 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  7 8 9
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 0 2 3 4 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  5 0 6
